---
import AppShell from '../layouts/AppShell.astro';
---

<AppShell title="Punjab GrainWatch — Methodology & Scientific Governance" activeNav="methodology">
  <div class="methodology-page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="header-breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Overview</a> / <span>Methodology & Governance</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="page-title">Methodology & Evidence Governance</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">
        Strict evidentiary standards governing the Punjab GrainWatch system under the AGENTS.md protocol.
        We report observable ground truth, document data gaps honestly, and strictly forbid simulated claims.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="methodology-content">
      <!-- Principle 1 -->
      <section class="method-card">
        <div class="card-num">01</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>Strict Prohibition on Hoarding Conclusions</h2>
          <p>
            Under Rule 6 of the core protocol, a statistical discrepancy or anomaly is strictly an <strong>investigation prompt</strong>,
            never an adjudication of commercial hoarding. Without continuous grain arrival observations, facility-level warehouse stock records,
            and legally adjudicated positive and negative controls, calculating actor-level hoarding probabilities or ranking named markets,
            traders, or mills as hoarders is mathematically and legally invalid.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Principle 2 -->
      <section class="method-card">
        <div class="card-num">02</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>No Grain Arrival Anomaly Proxies from Produce</h2>
          <p>
            The currently acquired mandi arrival panel (3,892 rows) covers 62 APMC produce commodities (vegetables, fruits, cash crops)
            with exactly <strong>zero wheat or paddy foodgrain rows</strong>. The 71 rows matching the substring "dhan" were empirically
            verified as Coriander Green (<em>Hara Dhaniya</em>). Under no circumstances may produce price or volume fluctuations be substituted
            or modeled as proxies for staple grain supply flows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Principle 3 -->
      <section class="method-card">
        <div class="card-num">03</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>Absence vs Zero Semantics</h2>
          <p>
            In accordance with Rule 5, <code>null</code>, unobserved, not reported, not applicable, and explicit source zero are treated as
            strictly distinct states. For example:
          </p>
          <ul class="method-list">
            <li><strong>AGMARKNET Paddy Prices:</strong> Arrival quantities are 100% null (not reported in weekly feed). They are preserved as nulls, not filled with zeros.</li>
            <li><strong>e-Mandikaran Price Sentinels:</strong> 3 records in the arrival panel contain <code>modal_price = 0.0</code> alongside positive min and max prices. These represent clerk sentinels for "modal price not reported", not zero-cost produce.</li>
            <li><strong>DFPD Buffer Stocks:</strong> State column is 100% null/NaN because the data represents India Central Pool aggregates, not state-level inventories.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Principle 4 -->
      <section class="method-card">
        <div class="card-num">04</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2>Decision Log `DECISION-20261022-01` (Schema Alignment)</h2>
          <p>
            Canonical schemas defined in <code>docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md</code> (v1.1.0) were calibrated to reflect actual physical CSV and GeoJSON
            structures discovered in the Phase 5 acquisition. Specifically:
          </p>
          <ul class="method-list">
            <li><strong>Crop Yield Year Coalescing:</strong> OGD rows populate <code>source_year_label</code> while DES APY rows populate <code>agricultural_year</code>. Coalescing these ensures unique candidate keys with 0 duplicate rows.</li>
            <li><strong>Procurement Temporal Basis:</strong> CFPP procurement rows represent 3 distinct temporal basis slices of date <code>2025-05-15</code> (target, single-day, cumulative) and must not be summed across rows.</li>
            <li><strong>Single Satellite Window:</strong> Copernicus Sentinel-2B tile is audited as a single 512x512 tile window from <code>2024-10-05</code>, not a continuous multi-temporal series.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppShell>

<style>
  .methodology-page {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .header-breadcrumbs {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .header-breadcrumbs a {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 800px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .methodology-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .method-card {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .card-num {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-wheat-500);
    opacity: 0.6;
    line-height: 1;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .card-body {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .card-body h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .card-body p {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .method-list {
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .method-list strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .method-card {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
